Shared ordinary-Jet fixture for all panes. Append the shown run() to these definitions; new A syntax remains proposed, not executed.

```jet
struct Tree {
    children: [Tree]
    cached_size: Int
}

fn deep_consistent(tree: Tree) Bool {
    count := 1
    loop child in tree.children {
        if !deep_consistent(child) -> return false
        count += child.cached_size
    }
    return tree.cached_size == count
}

fn sample_tree() Tree -> Tree{
    children: [Tree{children: [], cached_size: 1}, Tree{children: [], cached_size: 1}],
    cached_size: 3,
}

fn serve(tree: Tree) { print(tree.cached_size) }
```

Both examples use a package named tree. B additionally declares its setting in package.jet:

```jet
name: "tree"
version: "0.1.0"
settings: { deep_checks: Bool = false }
```

Both proposed runs corrupt the same cached root count from 3 to 4. Remove that assignment for the valid control. Off prints 4 for the corrupted tree; memory/type safety does not establish this logical count. On reports tree size is wrong before serve. The valid tree prints 3 in both selections. Existing effects and required guards remain enforced.

